{
  "about": "Envelope #12 of docs/share-a-server.md: only an admin device of the joining account accepts a share. #12 is signed by the per-share admin key shareAdmin = deriveShareAdminKey(memberUmk, shareId) (HKDF-SHA256, empty salt, info \"flagship/server-share-admin/v1|<shareId>\"), never by a stable account key (AT-LNK-10); `.com` attests that key when the account's sensitive key signs a `requests` envelope (flagship/share-key-attestation-request/v1|username|keyPubHex|issuedAt). Every platform must derive shareAdminPubHex (and otherShareAdminPubHex for otherShareId: a different key per share), build each envelope's and request's canonical string from `fields` and reproduce the Ed25519 signature with the named signer (adminRoot = Ed25519 seed adminRootSeedHex, irk = the protocol IRK of memberUmkSeedHex, member = deriveShareMemberKey(memberUmk, shareId)); refuse every `refuse` and `requestRefuse` case; fail to verify every `reject` case against the named public key; and parse `payload` (the sealed acceptance's plaintext) keeping its `admin` proof. `attestation` is `.com`'s CA-signed AccountKeyAttestation of the share key (CA = Ed25519 seed caSeedHex); only TS and the box check it, the apps carry it unchanged.",
